# Slab fills by state, indexed by the size bit then the anchor bit: one
# third or two thirds of the cell's height, anchored to its floor or its
# ceiling. The one-third rise is deliberately one stair tread — the
# auto-step threshold serves both. A ceiling slab is the floor one mirrored
# about the cell's mid-plane (pinned by a test), which keeps every pair the
# same volume, and so the same alchemy cost and the same dig.
version 1
shape slab
grid 12
states explicit 4
state 0                    # one third, floor
box all  0 0 0  12 4 12
state 1                    # two thirds, floor
box all  0 0 0  12 8 12
state 2                    # one third, ceiling
box all  0 8 0  12 12 12
state 3                    # two thirds, ceiling
box all  0 4 0  12 12 12
